{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:81613",
  "title": "Important: pcre2 security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-14 06:26:38"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-17 00:15:36"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The pcre2 package contains a new generation of the Perl Compatible Regular Expression libraries for implementing regular expression pattern matching using the same syntax and semantics as Perl. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* pcre2: PCRE2: Out-of-bounds write allows arbitrary code execution via crafted regular expressions (CVE-2026-86145)\n\n* pcre2: PCRE2: Out-of-bounds write via large pattern input (CVE-2026-89157)\n\n* PCRE2: PCRE2: Out-of-bounds write via integer overflow on 32-bit platforms (CVE-2026-89158)\n\n* pcre2: pcre2: Out-of-bounds write via crafted regular expression (CVE-2026-103111)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
